arnold_pipelines/megaplan/data/observe_skill.md:2:name: megaplan-observe
arnold_pipelines/megaplan/data/observe_skill.md:3:description: Observe an in-flight megaplan — introspect state, trace events, diagnose blockages, detect drift. Companion to megaplan-prep. Use during and after a run, not before.
arnold_pipelines/megaplan/data/observe_skill.md:6:# Megaplan Observe
arnold_pipelines/megaplan/data/observe_skill.md:8:When a megaplan is running — or stuck — `megaplan introspect`, `megaplan trace`, and `megaplan doctor` tell you *what it's doing, why, since when, and how to intervene*. This skill covers the observation surface; `megaplan-prep` covers profile/robustness/depth selection before a run.
arnold_pipelines/megaplan/data/observe_skill.md:14:`megaplan introspect --plan X` returns a single structured JSON payload. Four fields in it are the killers — each eliminates a failure mode that previously cost real sessions hours of confusion.
arnold_pipelines/megaplan/data/observe_skill.md:40:`megaplan/_core/workflow.py`, the runtime state-machine module that the
arnold_pipelines/megaplan/data/observe_skill.md:42:`megaplan override` will accept.
arnold_pipelines/megaplan/data/observe_skill.md:44:Important: `megaplan/_core/workflow.py` is not the authored workflow DSL source.
arnold_pipelines/megaplan/data/observe_skill.md:46:`arnold_pipelines/megaplan/workflows/workflow.py`.
arnold_pipelines/megaplan/data/observe_skill.md:50:If `rubric_doc.drift.missing_locally` is non-empty, the megaplan-prep skill references profile names your binary doesn't expose. This is the exact failure mode that wastes hours: the skill says `--profile thoughtful`, the binary says `Unknown profile 'thoughtful'`. `drift` catches it before the invocation. Use a profile from `profiles_available_locally` whose recipe matches what the rubric describes, or pin the binary to a state that has the canonical names.
arnold_pipelines/megaplan/data/observe_skill.md:56:When something seems wrong, investigate in this order:
arnold_pipelines/megaplan/data/observe_skill.md:58:1. **`megaplan introspect --plan X`** — one call, full picture. Always start here. The four killer fields answer 90% of questions.
arnold_pipelines/megaplan/data/observe_skill.md:59:2. **`megaplan trace --plan X --follow`** — if introspect says `progressing` but you want to watch. Stream events live; narrative format gives prose summaries of LLM calls.
arnold_pipelines/megaplan/data/observe_skill.md:60:3. **`megaplan doctor --plan X`** — if introspect shows a flag or state you don't recognise. Diagnostic checks with remediation hints.
arnold_pipelines/megaplan/data/observe_skill.md:65:When a run has a North Star, `introspect` includes an `anchors` summary. Use
arnold_pipelines/megaplan/data/observe_skill.md:66:`megaplan anchors show --plan X` to inspect the captured anchor text and metadata
arnold_pipelines/megaplan/data/observe_skill.md:76:### Stalled critique
arnold_pipelines/megaplan/data/observe_skill.md:83:- Check `block_details.outstanding_flags` — if the critique found flags it can't resolve, it may have looped without producing artifacts.
arnold_pipelines/megaplan/data/observe_skill.md:86:> *Session:* `prompt-registry-and-reminder-bundling-v5`, critique phase. 4 of 5 checks completed, last check at 14:25:11Z. At 14:55:00Z, `introspect` shows `liveness: quiet`, `last_artifact_rel: 29m 49s ago`. Subprocess PID 58800 still has an open TCP socket to Fireworks. `trace --follow --format narrative` shows: "Token stream stopped 28m ago. 4,200 tokens emitted at 18 tok/s. Last token at 14:26:31Z — no tokens since." The model finished producing but hermes didn't close the call — likely a provider-side hang. Kill the phase, `megaplan resume` picks up from where critique left off.
arnold_pipelines/megaplan/data/observe_skill.md:98:> *Session:* Plan went `blocked` at gate with 2 outstanding flags (FLAG-V4-001: high severity invariant contradiction, FLAG-V4-002: medium severity missing coverage). `recoverable_via` shows: `["fix brief and re-init (recommended)", "override add-note + override force-proceed", "override replan (requires state ∈ {critiqued, failed, finalized, gated})"]`. FLAG-V4-001 is a genuine correctness issue — fix the brief to resolve the contradiction, re-init. FLAG-V4-002 is acceptable — the uncovered module is out of scope per the brief. Add a note documenting the scope decision, then `override force-proceed`.
arnold_pipelines/megaplan/data/observe_skill.md:107:- Run `megaplan doctor --repo` before `megaplan init` to catch this proactively.
arnold_pipelines/megaplan/data/observe_skill.md:110:> *Session:* `megaplan init --profile thoughtful` → `Unknown profile 'thoughtful'`. `introspect` (on a different plan) shows `rubric_doc.drift.missing_locally: ["basic","led","thoughtful","super-premium"]`, `profiles_available_locally: ["solo","directed","partnered","premium","apex"]`. The binary is on branch `sprint-a-base` which renamed the canonical profiles to the new 5-tier scheme. The skill doc hasn't been updated yet. Use `--profile partnered` (the tier-3 equivalent) or switch to main where the old names still exist.
arnold_pipelines/megaplan/data/observe_skill.md:126:### Rule 3: Do not stash / checkout in the megaplan source repo without user consent — editable installs make repo state load-bearing
arnold_pipelines/megaplan/data/observe_skill.md:128:If megaplan is installed via `pip install -e .`, any branch switch or uncommitted change in the source tree changes behavior immediately. `megaplan doctor --repo` surfaces this. Stashing, checking out, or pulling without explicit user consent can silently remove the profile a caller is about to invoke.
arnold_pipelines/megaplan/data/observe_skill.md:140:User asks whether a long-running plan is still progressing.
arnold_pipelines/megaplan/data/observe_skill.md:143:megaplan introspect --plan prompt-registry-and-reminder-bundling-v5
arnold_pipelines/megaplan/data/observe_skill.md:146:Read `active_phase.liveness`. If `progressing`: "Yes — critique is still running. Last artifact 3 minutes ago (critique_check_scope.json). Model claude:opus-4.7 is actively producing tokens." If `quiet`: "Critique hasn't produced an artifact in 8 minutes, but the LLM call is still in-flight. Watching." If `stalled`: "Critique appears to have stopped — no events in 12 minutes and no in-flight LLM call. Check `recoverable_via`."
arnold_pipelines/megaplan/data/observe_skill.md:151:megaplan introspect --plan my-sprint
arnold_pipelines/megaplan/data/observe_skill.md:154:Read `block_details.recoverable_via`. Execute the first applicable option. Verify the state transition succeeded with another `introspect` call. If the override was `force-proceed`, confirm `state` is now past `blocked`. If the override was `replan`, confirm the plan re-entered the planning phase.
arnold_pipelines/megaplan/data/observe_skill.md:159:megaplan trace --plan my-sprint --format narrative --since 10m
arnold_pipelines/megaplan/data/observe_skill.md:162:The narrative format groups consecutive LLM calls into prose summaries. Look for which model is being called, how frequently, and at what token volume. Cross-reference against the tier's expected cost profile from `megaplan-prep`. If the model is correct but call frequency is high, the plan may be looping — check `phase_retry` events. If the model is wrong (e.g., premium model on a solo-tier phase), check for an unintended `override set-profile`.
arnold_pipelines/megaplan/data/observe_skill.md:164:### "I switched branches and now megaplan is broken"
arnold_pipelines/megaplan/data/observe_skill.md:167:megaplan doctor --repo
arnold_pipelines/megaplan/data/observe_skill.md:170:The repo-level check catches: rubric/binary drift (skill references profiles the current binary doesn't have), editable-install + dirty working tree (uncommitted changes affecting behavior), skill files out of sync with installed copies. Fix the specific WARN/ERROR lines before running any plan.
arnold_pipelines/megaplan/data/observe_skill.md:175:megaplan introspect --plan X
arnold_pipelines/megaplan/data/observe_skill.md:187:If nothing jumps out, escalate to `trace --follow` to watch live, then `doctor --plan` for diagnostic checks.
