arnold_pipelines/megaplan/data/bakeoff_skill.md:2:name: megaplan-bakeoff
arnold_pipelines/megaplan/data/bakeoff_skill.md:3:description: Methodology for running multi-profile LLM bake-offs via megaplan and presenting fair, blind-assessed comparisons. Cost/quality discipline, prompt hygiene, pre-merge gates, and reporting patterns. Use when the user says "bakeoff", "bake off", "megaplan bakeoff", or asks to compare profile mixes head-to-head.
arnold_pipelines/megaplan/data/bakeoff_skill.md:8:A bake-off runs the same task through N profiles concurrently and picks a winner. Use it to test profile mixes (which model leads, who critiques, who executes), to evaluate cost-quality trade-offs, or to compare codebases head-to-head. This skill captures the operational knowledge that separates "well-run bake-off" from "expensive shrug."
arnold_pipelines/megaplan/data/bakeoff_skill.md:20:Built-in profiles (megaplan): `standard`, `all-claude`, `kimi`, `claude-kimi-deepseek`. Project-local in `<project>/.megaplan/profiles.toml`.
arnold_pipelines/megaplan/data/bakeoff_skill.md:23:- **Who leads** (plan/revise/finalize): Claude vs DeepSeek vs all-X
arnold_pipelines/megaplan/data/bakeoff_skill.md:24:- **Who critiques**: Claude tends to add disproportionate value as a critic
arnold_pipelines/megaplan/data/bakeoff_skill.md:34:2. Catches Fireworks streaming bug (`max_tokens > 4096` requires `stream=true`) — fixed in current megaplan but always worth verifying.
arnold_pipelines/megaplan/data/bakeoff_skill.md:41:**Do NOT include absolute paths in the idea text.** Specifically: never write `Project: /abs/path/to/repo` or any equivalent. Megaplan injects its own `Project directory: <worktree>` line. If your idea text has a competing path, models will trust the user-authored line and execute against the wrong directory.
arnold_pipelines/megaplan/data/bakeoff_skill.md:43:Symptom when this happens: bakeoff arm reports `final_state: done` but `git -C <worktree> diff main --stat` is empty. Files appear in your *main* repo instead, polluting it. Megaplan's audit catches this (`files_in_diff: []` while `files_claimed` is non-empty) but light-robustness review auto-approves it anyway.
arnold_pipelines/megaplan/data/bakeoff_skill.md:47:- Megaplan ≥ commit `a0ed9f51` (sandbox fix) enforces this at the tool layer — any `cd /escape && ...` is refused.
arnold_pipelines/megaplan/data/bakeoff_skill.md:48:- Always pre-merge gate (below).
arnold_pipelines/megaplan/data/bakeoff_skill.md:53:PYENV_VERSION=3.11.11 python -m arnold_pipelines.megaplan bakeoff run \
arnold_pipelines/megaplan/data/bakeoff_skill.md:55:  --profiles all-claude deepseek-kimi-deepseek claude-kimi-deepseek-or all-deepseek-or deepseek-claude-critique \
arnold_pipelines/megaplan/data/bakeoff_skill.md:64:Light robustness loop: plan → critique → revise → finalize → execute → review. No prep, no gate.
arnold_pipelines/megaplan/data/bakeoff_skill.md:71:- The `bakeoff status` table can lag — last write to state.json is the truth. Check `<worktree>/.megaplan/plans/<plan>/state.json`'s `current_state` field if status seems stuck.
arnold_pipelines/megaplan/data/bakeoff_skill.md:73:## Pre-merge gate (don't trust outcome.json alone)
arnold_pipelines/megaplan/data/bakeoff_skill.md:79:  d=/Users/.../.megaplan-worktrees/<exp-id>/$p
arnold_pipelines/megaplan/data/bakeoff_skill.md:103:5. Forbid the sub-agent from peeking at `.megaplan/` files inside worktrees (those reveal the profile via plan_v2.md or state.json).
arnold_pipelines/megaplan/data/bakeoff_skill.md:117:- **Role specialization findings** (e.g. "Claude as critic raises non-Claude plans by a full grade")
arnold_pipelines/megaplan/data/bakeoff_skill.md:127:PYENV_VERSION=3.11.11 python -m arnold_pipelines.megaplan bakeoff compare --exp <id>  # required before pick
arnold_pipelines/megaplan/data/bakeoff_skill.md:128:PYENV_VERSION=3.11.11 python -m arnold_pipelines.megaplan bakeoff pick --exp <id> --profile <winner> --rationale "..."
arnold_pipelines/megaplan/data/bakeoff_skill.md:129:PYENV_VERSION=3.11.11 python -m arnold_pipelines.megaplan bakeoff merge --exp <id>
arnold_pipelines/megaplan/data/bakeoff_skill.md:132:Merge brings the winner's worktree changes into main as uncommitted edits — review, run pytest, then commit yourself. Don't auto-commit blindly; the merge step doesn't run tests.
arnold_pipelines/megaplan/data/bakeoff_skill.md:145:- **Stuck arm**: check `ps aux | grep megaplan` and `lsof -p <pid> | grep TCP` — if no socket activity, kill and re-launch single-profile via `megaplan auto`.
arnold_pipelines/megaplan/data/bakeoff_skill.md:146:- **Empty critique output**: check `<plan>/critique_v1_raw.txt` for HTTP errors. Fireworks 400 streaming bug pattern: "max_tokens > 4096 must have stream=true". Megaplan ≥ `c2bbc729` fixes this.
arnold_pipelines/megaplan/data/bakeoff_skill.md:147:- **Stale `bakeoff status` table**: check actual `outcome.json` files in `~/.megaplan/bakeoffs/<exp>/<profile>/` — those are authoritative when the run completes.
arnold_pipelines/megaplan/data/bakeoff_skill.md:153:- Critique returned `{"checks": [], "flags": []}` and state stuck at `planned` (silent worker failure).
arnold_pipelines/megaplan/data/bakeoff_skill.md:156:`megaplan bakeoff abandon --exp <id>` discards worktrees but keeps audit data for forensics.
