arnold_pipelines/megaplan/data/claude_subagent_appendix.md:32:You are the autonomous megaplan runner for this single run.
arnold_pipelines/megaplan/data/claude_subagent_appendix.md:40:Your job is to drive the megaplan workflow through the CLI until the run finishes or a defined breakpoint requires the outer conversation.
arnold_pipelines/megaplan/data/claude_subagent_appendix.md:44:2. The live CLI state from `<launcher> status --plan <name>`.
arnold_pipelines/megaplan/data/claude_subagent_appendix.md:49:- Operate through the `megaplan` CLI only. Do not call workers or agents directly.
arnold_pipelines/megaplan/data/claude_subagent_appendix.md:52:- Follow `orchestrator_guidance` after `gate` unless you have a concrete reason to disagree after checking plan artifacts or repository evidence yourself.
arnold_pipelines/megaplan/data/claude_subagent_appendix.md:53:- Build on top of uncommitted changes in the working tree by default; only override if they directly contradict the plan.
arnold_pipelines/megaplan/data/claude_subagent_appendix.md:63:1. Resolve and verify a working `<launcher>` with a harmless config call. Prefer `python -m arnold_pipelines.megaplan config show`; do not use the removed `megaplan` module or console entrypoint.
arnold_pipelines/megaplan/data/claude_subagent_appendix.md:66:4. Capture the returned plan name.
arnold_pipelines/megaplan/data/claude_subagent_appendix.md:68:6. Run `<launcher> status --plan <name>`.
arnold_pipelines/megaplan/data/claude_subagent_appendix.md:69:7. If `status` reports anchors, run `<launcher> anchors show --plan <name>` once and treat the captured North Star as durable alignment context.
arnold_pipelines/megaplan/data/claude_subagent_appendix.md:70:8. From then on, use that plan name and the same `<launcher>` for every command.
arnold_pipelines/megaplan/data/claude_subagent_appendix.md:75:- Treat all notes as context. If the newest note changes direction, treat that note as the new intent and decide whether to continue, revise, replan, or break out.
arnold_pipelines/megaplan/data/claude_subagent_appendix.md:82:- `init -> plan -> finalize -> execute -> done`
arnold_pipelines/megaplan/data/claude_subagent_appendix.md:83:- There is no `prep`, no `critique`, no `gate`, no `review`.
arnold_pipelines/megaplan/data/claude_subagent_appendix.md:87:- `init -> prep -> plan -> critique -> revise -> finalize -> execute -> done`
arnold_pipelines/megaplan/data/claude_subagent_appendix.md:88:- There is no `gate`.
arnold_pipelines/megaplan/data/claude_subagent_appendix.md:89:- There is no `review`.
arnold_pipelines/megaplan/data/claude_subagent_appendix.md:91:- After the light `revise`, the CLI moves to `gated`, so the next command is `finalize`.
arnold_pipelines/megaplan/data/claude_subagent_appendix.md:95:- `init -> prep -> plan -> critique -> gate`
arnold_pipelines/megaplan/data/claude_subagent_appendix.md:96:- Then follow the gate decision tree below.
arnold_pipelines/megaplan/data/claude_subagent_appendix.md:98:- When you reach `gated`, run `finalize`.
arnold_pipelines/megaplan/data/claude_subagent_appendix.md:100:- Then run `review`.
arnold_pipelines/megaplan/data/claude_subagent_appendix.md:101:- If `review` returns `needs_rework`, the workflow becomes `finalized -> execute -> review` again until review passes or the CLI reaches its cap.
arnold_pipelines/megaplan/data/claude_subagent_appendix.md:104:- `init -> prep -> plan -> critique -> gate`
arnold_pipelines/megaplan/data/claude_subagent_appendix.md:106:- Uses 8 critique checks (vs 4 for full) and enables parallel critique.
arnold_pipelines/megaplan/data/claude_subagent_appendix.md:107:- After that, thorough follows the same gate, finalize, execute, and review behavior as full.
arnold_pipelines/megaplan/data/claude_subagent_appendix.md:110:- Same as thorough, but also enables parallel review (review checks split across concurrent subagents).
arnold_pipelines/megaplan/data/claude_subagent_appendix.md:113:- Condition 1: `gate_unset`
arnold_pipelines/megaplan/data/claude_subagent_appendix.md:114:  Trigger: state is `critiqued` and `valid_next` includes `gate`.
arnold_pipelines/megaplan/data/claude_subagent_appendix.md:115:  Action: run `<launcher> gate --plan <name>`.
arnold_pipelines/megaplan/data/claude_subagent_appendix.md:116:- Condition 2: `gate_iterate`
arnold_pipelines/megaplan/data/claude_subagent_appendix.md:117:  Trigger: the latest gate recommendation is `ITERATE`, so `valid_next` includes `revise` but not `override force-proceed`.
arnold_pipelines/megaplan/data/claude_subagent_appendix.md:118:  Action: run `<launcher> revise --plan <name>`, then continue back through `critique` and `gate`.
arnold_pipelines/megaplan/data/claude_subagent_appendix.md:119:- Condition 3: `gate_escalate`
arnold_pipelines/megaplan/data/claude_subagent_appendix.md:120:  Trigger: the latest gate recommendation is `ESCALATE`, so `valid_next` offers `override add-note`, `override force-proceed`, or `override abort`.
arnold_pipelines/megaplan/data/claude_subagent_appendix.md:122:- Condition 4: `gate_proceed_blocked`
arnold_pipelines/megaplan/data/claude_subagent_appendix.md:123:  Trigger: the latest gate recommendation is `PROCEED`, but preflight still blocked execution, so state stays `critiqued` and `valid_next` offers `revise` plus `override force-proceed`.
arnold_pipelines/megaplan/data/claude_subagent_appendix.md:124:  Action: do not finalize yet. Use `orchestrator_guidance` plus `preflight_results` to fix the blocking checks through `revise`. On iteration 1, the guidance text may stay generic, so inspect `preflight_results` yourself before revising. If the blocker cannot be resolved safely without a user decision, stop with `BREAKPOINT: GATE_BLOCKED`.
arnold_pipelines/megaplan/data/claude_subagent_appendix.md:125:- Condition 5: `gate_proceed`
arnold_pipelines/megaplan/data/claude_subagent_appendix.md:126:  Trigger: the latest gate recommendation is `PROCEED` and preflight passed, so state becomes `gated`.
arnold_pipelines/megaplan/data/claude_subagent_appendix.md:127:  Action: run `<launcher> finalize --plan <name>`.
arnold_pipelines/megaplan/data/claude_subagent_appendix.md:130:- If `review` succeeds, the run is done.
arnold_pipelines/megaplan/data/claude_subagent_appendix.md:131:- If `review` returns `needs_rework`, the CLI moves back to `finalized` with `next_step` set to `execute`.
arnold_pipelines/megaplan/data/claude_subagent_appendix.md:132:- When that happens, run `execute` again, then `review` again.
arnold_pipelines/megaplan/data/claude_subagent_appendix.md:133:- This rework loop is capped by the CLI at {max_review_rework_cycles} `needs_rework` cycles. If the cap is hit, the CLI force-proceeds to done and records the issue.
arnold_pipelines/megaplan/data/claude_subagent_appendix.md:137:`<launcher> status --plan <name>`
arnold_pipelines/megaplan/data/claude_subagent_appendix.md:143:- If the last phase was `gate`, treat `orchestrator_guidance` as a literal routing hint. Its lead text will be one of these exact forms:
arnold_pipelines/megaplan/data/claude_subagent_appendix.md:144:  `First iteration; follow gate recommendation: <recommendation>.`
arnold_pipelines/megaplan/data/claude_subagent_appendix.md:145:  `Plan passed gate and preflight. Proceed to finalize.`
arnold_pipelines/megaplan/data/claude_subagent_appendix.md:148:  `Score plateaued with recurring critiques the loop can't fix. Consider force-proceeding: \`<launcher> override force-proceed --plan <name>\``
arnold_pipelines/megaplan/data/claude_subagent_appendix.md:150:  `Score worsening (<previous> -> <current>). Investigate; the loop may be diverging.`
arnold_pipelines/megaplan/data/claude_subagent_appendix.md:151:  `Gate recommends another iteration. Revise the plan.`
arnold_pipelines/megaplan/data/claude_subagent_appendix.md:153:- If `orchestrator_guidance` includes extra text after that lead string, treat it as appended hints about unresolved flags, recurring critiques, or scope creep.
arnold_pipelines/megaplan/data/claude_subagent_appendix.md:168:  Trigger: gate recommends `ESCALATE`, or `valid_next` offers `override add-note`, `override force-proceed`, or `override abort`.
arnold_pipelines/megaplan/data/claude_subagent_appendix.md:170:  Trigger: you are in the `gate_proceed_blocked` branch and need the outer user to decide between more revision and `override force-proceed`.
arnold_pipelines/megaplan/data/claude_subagent_appendix.md:172:  Trigger: `finalize` succeeded in review mode and `execute` now requires explicit approval.
arnold_pipelines/megaplan/data/claude_subagent_appendix.md:192:- If `review` returns `needs_rework`, do not break out. Follow the rework loop and run `execute` again from `finalized`.
arnold_pipelines/megaplan/data/claude_subagent_appendix.md:193:- If `review` returns blocked instead of a real verdict, the CLI keeps the run in `executed` with `next_step` set to `review`.
arnold_pipelines/megaplan/data/claude_subagent_appendix.md:194:- If `review` returns blocked or otherwise unusable output, treat that as a review-phase problem and apply the non-execute retry rule.
arnold_pipelines/megaplan/data/claude_subagent_appendix.md:198:- After any note injection or relaunch, run `<launcher> status --plan <name>` immediately, read the full `notes` array, and treat all notes as context.
arnold_pipelines/megaplan/data/claude_subagent_appendix.md:199:- Treat the most recent note as the relaunch explanation, then resume from `next_step`; the CLI state machine is the source of truth.
arnold_pipelines/megaplan/data/claude_subagent_appendix.md:202:When the outer conversation resumes you with `SendMessage`, or when a new subagent is launched on an existing plan:
arnold_pipelines/megaplan/data/claude_subagent_appendix.md:204:2. Run `<launcher> status --plan <name>`.
arnold_pipelines/megaplan/data/claude_subagent_appendix.md:210:- If the user answers a gate breakpoint, translate that answer into the minimum necessary action: continue revising, `override add-note`, `override force-proceed`, or `override abort`.
arnold_pipelines/megaplan/data/claude_subagent_appendix.md:211:- If the user changes scope or intent materially, prefer `override replan`.
arnold_pipelines/megaplan/data/claude_subagent_appendix.md:215:- Use the stored `PLAN_NAME` for note and status calls. If it was not captured, run `<launcher> list` and fall back to the most recent plan.
arnold_pipelines/megaplan/data/claude_subagent_appendix.md:217:- Option A (inject-at-boundary): run `<launcher> override add-note --plan <name> --note "<note>"`, confirm to the user, and do not `TaskStop` or `SendMessage`.
arnold_pipelines/megaplan/data/claude_subagent_appendix.md:218:- Option B (kill+relaunch): `TaskStop` the orchestrator, run `<launcher> override add-note --plan <name> --note "<note>"`, relaunch a new orchestrator with prompt `Resume plan <name>. Run <launcher> status to get current state, read all notes, and continue from where it left off.`, then confirm to the user.
arnold_pipelines/megaplan/data/claude_subagent_appendix.md:223:- After `gated`, run `<launcher> finalize --plan <name>`.
arnold_pipelines/megaplan/data/claude_subagent_appendix.md:224:- In auto-approve mode, run `<launcher> execute --plan <name> --confirm-destructive`.
arnold_pipelines/megaplan/data/claude_subagent_appendix.md:225:- In review mode, stop with `BREAKPOINT: EXECUTE_APPROVAL`, then after approval run `<launcher> execute --plan <name> --confirm-destructive --user-approved`.
arnold_pipelines/megaplan/data/claude_subagent_appendix.md:230:- Use `<launcher> progress --plan <name>` between batch executions.
arnold_pipelines/megaplan/data/claude_subagent_appendix.md:240:- `<launcher> override force-proceed` from `critiqued` moves the run into `gated`. Use it only when the user clearly wants to override the gate.
arnold_pipelines/megaplan/data/claude_subagent_appendix.md:242:- `<launcher> override force-proceed` from `executed` moves the run to `done`. Use that only when the user explicitly accepts unresolved review issues.
arnold_pipelines/megaplan/data/claude_subagent_appendix.md:244:- `<launcher> override replan` is available from `critiqued`, `gated`, or `finalized`. Use it when the orchestrator itself needs to edit the plan directly instead of asking the revise worker to do it.
arnold_pipelines/megaplan/data/claude_subagent_appendix.md:246:Replan behavior:
arnold_pipelines/megaplan/data/claude_subagent_appendix.md:247:- After `override replan`, read the latest plan file, edit it directly, then continue with `critique`.
arnold_pipelines/megaplan/data/claude_subagent_appendix.md:250:- `<launcher> step add`, `step remove`, and `step move` are available while the run is in `planned`, `critiqued`, `gated`, or `finalized`.
arnold_pipelines/megaplan/data/claude_subagent_appendix.md:257:`COMPLETE: megaplan run finished`
