arnold_pipelines/megaplan/data/tickets_skill.md:2:name: megaplan-tickets
arnold_pipelines/megaplan/data/tickets_skill.md:3:description: File and manage megaplan tickets — short, repo-scoped notes on problems or observations that get folded into epics and auto-addressed when the resolving epic completes.
arnold_pipelines/megaplan/data/tickets_skill.md:6:# Megaplan tickets
arnold_pipelines/megaplan/data/tickets_skill.md:8:Tickets are short, repo-scoped notes on problems, bugs, or "we should look at this" observations against a codebase. They live as committed `.md` files under `<repo>/.megaplan/tickets/` and (when a cloud store is configured) mirror to `tickets` / `ticket_epics` tables. Tickets are inert until folded into an epic — they capture problems, not work.
arnold_pipelines/megaplan/data/tickets_skill.md:12:Reach for `megaplan ticket new` when:
arnold_pipelines/megaplan/data/tickets_skill.md:13:- During epic or plan execution you notice an **out-of-scope problem** that should be tracked but isn't blocking the current task.
arnold_pipelines/megaplan/data/tickets_skill.md:18:- Guidance/corrections to *how the tooling itself behaves* — that's `megaplan feedback` (a separate, plan-scoped concept).
arnold_pipelines/megaplan/data/tickets_skill.md:25:megaplan ticket new "<title>" -b "<body>" [--tags tag1,tag2]
arnold_pipelines/megaplan/data/tickets_skill.md:32:- `source` is auto-derived: if `MEGAPLAN_TURN_ID` is set (the agent is running under a megaplan-launched worker), `source=agent` and the turn id is recorded; otherwise `source=human`.
arnold_pipelines/megaplan/data/tickets_skill.md:37:cat <<'EOF' | megaplan ticket new "Title here" --tags tag1,tag2 -
arnold_pipelines/megaplan/data/tickets_skill.md:47:megaplan ticket list   [--status open|addressed|dismissed] [--tags t1,t2] [--json]
arnold_pipelines/megaplan/data/tickets_skill.md:48:megaplan ticket show   <id> [--json]
arnold_pipelines/megaplan/data/tickets_skill.md:49:megaplan ticket search [KW ...] [--all] [--project P]... [--all-projects]
arnold_pipelines/megaplan/data/tickets_skill.md:61:- **Scope** — current repo. Pass `--all-projects` to scan every known repo (locally: the auto-maintained `~/.config/megaplan/known_repos.json` registry; cloud: every codebase). Pass `--project PATH|owner/name|name` (repeatable) to scope to specific repos.
arnold_pipelines/megaplan/data/tickets_skill.md:70:megaplan ticket search stderr timeout
arnold_pipelines/megaplan/data/tickets_skill.md:73:megaplan ticket search stderr timeout --all
arnold_pipelines/megaplan/data/tickets_skill.md:76:megaplan ticket search redis --all-projects --status open --sort length --json
arnold_pipelines/megaplan/data/tickets_skill.md:79:megaplan ticket search auth --project ~/Documents/reigh-app --project banodoco/megaplan
arnold_pipelines/megaplan/data/tickets_skill.md:85:megaplan ticket edit    <id> [--title ...] [--body ...] [--status ...] [--add-tag ...] [--remove-tag ...]
arnold_pipelines/megaplan/data/tickets_skill.md:86:megaplan ticket link    <ticket> <epic> [--resolves]
arnold_pipelines/megaplan/data/tickets_skill.md:87:megaplan ticket unlink  <ticket> <epic>
arnold_pipelines/megaplan/data/tickets_skill.md:88:megaplan ticket addressed <id> [--note "..."]
arnold_pipelines/megaplan/data/tickets_skill.md:89:megaplan ticket dismiss   <id> [--reason "..."]
arnold_pipelines/megaplan/data/tickets_skill.md:90:megaplan ticket reopen    <id>
arnold_pipelines/megaplan/data/tickets_skill.md:97:Megaplan runs in one of two modes; tickets work transparently in both:
arnold_pipelines/megaplan/data/tickets_skill.md:100:- **Cloud-configured** (`SUPABASE_DB_URL` or megaplan config points at a store) — every operation writes the `.md` file **and** mirrors to the `tickets` / `ticket_epics` tables. Auto-registers the codebase on first ticket if needed.
arnold_pipelines/megaplan/data/tickets_skill.md:107:<repo>/.megaplan/tickets/{ulid}-{slug}.md
arnold_pipelines/megaplan/data/tickets_skill.md:131:## Discovery at planning time
arnold_pipelines/megaplan/data/tickets_skill.md:133:When a new epic is created or refined for the current repo, the planner automatically surfaces open tickets ranked by tag overlap with the epic's goal and recency. The planner may propose links with `resolves_on_complete=true`. You don't need to remind it — discovery is built into the plan-phase prompt assembly.
arnold_pipelines/megaplan/data/tickets_skill.md:139:| File a ticket | `megaplan ticket new "title" -b "body" [--tags t1,t2]` |
arnold_pipelines/megaplan/data/tickets_skill.md:140:| Pipe a multi-line body | `cat body.md \| megaplan ticket new "title" -` |
arnold_pipelines/megaplan/data/tickets_skill.md:141:| List open tickets | `megaplan ticket list --status open --json` |
arnold_pipelines/megaplan/data/tickets_skill.md:142:| Search by keyword in this repo | `megaplan ticket search foo bar` |
arnold_pipelines/megaplan/data/tickets_skill.md:143:| Search across every repo | `megaplan ticket search foo --all-projects` |
arnold_pipelines/megaplan/data/tickets_skill.md:144:| Link a ticket to an epic so it auto-closes | `megaplan ticket link <tid> <eid> --resolves` |
arnold_pipelines/megaplan/data/tickets_skill.md:145:| Mark addressed manually | `megaplan ticket addressed <tid> --note "..."` |
arnold_pipelines/megaplan/data/tickets_skill.md:146:| Reopen a closed ticket | `megaplan ticket reopen <tid>` |
arnold_pipelines/megaplan/pipelines/epic-blitz/prompts/low/migration_backcompat.md:1:You are a **low-abstraction critic** focused on **migration and backward compatibility**. Your role is to assess whether the epic's changes preserve existing plan directories, critique schemas, robustness behavior, profiles, and chain specs.
arnold_pipelines/megaplan/pipelines/epic-blitz/prompts/low/migration_backcompat.md:3:You are working from the **latest revised epic artifact** (not the original draft). The artifact you receive already incorporates revisions from prior critique rounds.
arnold_pipelines/megaplan/pipelines/epic-blitz/prompts/low/migration_backcompat.md:9:1. **Plan directory compatibility** — will existing plan directories (with `.megaplan/` artifacts from older runs) still work after these changes?
arnold_pipelines/megaplan/pipelines/epic-blitz/prompts/low/migration_backcompat.md:10:2. **Schema backward compatibility** — will existing critique schemas, verdict formats, or artifact layouts remain readable?
arnold_pipelines/megaplan/pipelines/epic-blitz/prompts/low/migration_backcompat.md:42:**Revised epic to review:**
arnold_pipelines/megaplan/pipelines/epic-blitz/prompts/high/existing_system_reuse.md:3:You are working from the **latest revised epic artifact** (not the original draft). The artifact you receive already incorporates revisions from prior critique rounds.
arnold_pipelines/megaplan/pipelines/epic-blitz/prompts/high/existing_system_reuse.md:40:**Epic to review:**
arnold_pipelines/megaplan/pipelines/epic-blitz/prompts/high/missing_abstraction.md:3:You are working from the **latest revised epic artifact** (not the original draft). The artifact you receive already incorporates revisions from prior critique rounds.
arnold_pipelines/megaplan/pipelines/epic-blitz/prompts/high/missing_abstraction.md:12:4. **Missing shared infrastructure** — are multiple milestones each planning to build their own version of something (validation, error handling, artifact layout) that should be centralized?
arnold_pipelines/megaplan/pipelines/epic-blitz/prompts/high/missing_abstraction.md:40:**Epic to review:**
