     1	"""Chain driver — run a pipeline of milestone plans with state kept in megaplan.
     2	
     3	This replaces ad-hoc bash orchestration (`chain.sh`). A YAML spec declares an
     4	optional seed plan and an ordered list of milestones; each milestone is
     5	initialized from an idea file, then driven to `done` via the same auto-loop
     6	entry point used by `megaplan auto`.
     7	
     8	Plan state stays in megaplan. Bash is no longer responsible for polling or
     9	deciding the next step — only for process/container liveness.
    10	
    11	Spec format (YAML)::
    12	
    13	    base_branch: main
    14	    seed:
    15	      plan: milestone-m0-from-docs-state-20260415-0217
    16	    milestones:
    17	      - label: m1
    18	        idea: /workspace/ideas/M1-foundation-store.txt
    19	        branch: megaplan/m1-foundation-store   # optional, currently informational
    20	        profile: thoughtful                     # optional init rubric knobs
    21	        robustness: standard
    22	        vendor: claude
    23	        depth: high
    24	        critic: kimi
    25	        with_prep: true
    26	        with_feedback: true
    27	        prep_direction: |               # optional steering for the prep phase
    28	          focus on the worker shutdown path and how cancel signals propagate
    29	          to inflight tasks; skip CLI plumbing.
    30	        deepseek_provider: direct
    31	      - label: m1a
    32	        idea: /workspace/ideas/M1a-settings-store.txt
    33	    on_failure:
    34	      abort: stop_chain          # stop_chain | skip_milestone | retry_milestone
    35	    on_escalate:
    36	      abort: stop_chain          # stop_chain | skip_milestone | retry_milestone
    37	
    38	Progress is persisted under ``.megaplan/plans/.chains/`` so a relaunched
    39	process can resume where the previous run left off without dirtying milestone
    40	branches.
    41	"""
